<title>UK: Yorks Elec up on reports of share buyback.</title>
<headline>Yorks Elec up on reports of share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yorkshire Electric jumped 14p to 755p by 0825 GMT, on press reports the company was considering a share buyback or a special dividend, traders said.  </p>
<p>The Financial Times, quoting the electricity group's finance director Tony Coleman, said the company was contemplating a 120 million stg share buyback or paying a special dividend.</p>
<p>He was also quoted as saying Yorkshire planned to increse its gearing from about 45 percent to 100 percent this year.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
